\section{Experiments}
\label{sec:results}

We evaluate on two environments. \emph{Snake} $5\times5$ is a reactive navigation task
with a moderately sparse reward (food and death). \emph{Pac-Man} on procedurally
randomised layouts adds partial observability, a persistent mismatch between the fixed
action set and the legal moves, and rewards spanning several magnitudes. In every task
the agent sees only a small egocentric grid, Poisson rate-coded into input spikes
(Appendix~\ref{app:impl}).

\pending{: \textbf{Versioning note.} The e-prop baselines are being rerun with the
reward-based learning signal implemented as described in Appendix~\ref{app:impl}; every
comparison involving them, and every figure below, is a placeholder until then.}

The learner is an excitatory--inhibitory recurrent SRNN of ALIF neurons with
sparse, spatially structured connectivity, trained \emph{strictly online}, with
episodic learning signals and a never-reset network state as defined in
Section~\ref{sec:intro}. Each output
head is optionally preceded by a non-recurrent \emph{field} layer that lengthens
the causal path from input to output, which we use to stress-test how each rule
scales with that path. The network runs on the event-driven GeNN
simulator~\citep{Yavuz2016GeNN}; architecture, connectivity, initialisation, and
all hyperparameters are given in Appendices~\ref{app:arch}--\ref{app:hyper}.

We compare \method{}, the rule of Eq.~\eqref{eq:distributed-update} with the
decorrelation reward of Eq.~\eqref{eq:decorr} (and, where stated, with the centred
drift and the homeostat instead), with reward-based e-prop using \emph{random}, \emph{adaptive}
and \emph{symmetric} feedback, and with a \emph{reservoir}, inspired by liquid state
machines~\citep{Maass2002LSM}, whose input and recurrent weights stay at their initial
values so that only the readout learns. The reservoir measures how much of the
performance requires learning in the hidden layers at all. All rules share the readout
rule, the optimiser and the per-timestep schedule. Hyperparameters were explored within
a limited budget, so a rule that fails to learn here is one for which we found no
working configuration, not one that cannot learn. Primary comparisons average
\pending{3--5} seeds.

